"Now let me check if there are any existing test files", "parent_progress_item_id": "6a894bed-3ac4-4308-962c-a2bdfaa4c974", "__event_type__": "UserVisibleModelOutputEvent"}, {"timestamp": 1760777936.894273, "tool_name": "mcp__codespeak__ls", "title": "mcp__codespeak__ls", "details": null, "parent_progress_item_id": "6a894bed-3ac4-4308-962c-a2bdfaa4c974", "__event_type__": "ToolCallEvent"}, {"timestamp": 1760777941.17891, "text": "The tests directory is empty, so I need to create a test file. Based on the `<tests_to_add>` specification, I need to create a unit test for the `main` function in `src/test_build/main.py`.\n\nLet me create a test file for this", "parent_progress_item_id": "6a894bed-3ac4-4308-962c-a2bdfaa4c974", "__event_type__": "UserVisibleModelOutputEvent"}, {"timestamp": 1760777943.9285216, "tool_name": "Write", "title": "write [tests]/test_main.py", "details": "{\n  \"file_path\": \"/codespeak/test-build/tests/test_main.py\",\n  \"content\": \"\\\"\\\"\\\"Unit tests for main module.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport pytest\\nfrom io import StringIO\\nfrom unittest.mock import patch\\n\\nfrom test_build.main import main\\n\\n\\nclass TestMain:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Test cases for the main function.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    @pytest.mark.timeout(30)\\n    def test_main(self):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Test main function - unit_tests for main\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        # Capture stdout to verify the output\\n        with patch('sys.stdout', new_callable=StringIO) as mock_stdout:\\n            main()\\n            output = mock_stdout.getvalue()\\n\\n        # Assert that \\\"Hello\\\" is printed followed by a newline\\n        assert output == \\\"Hello\\\\n\\\"\"\n}", "parent_progress_item_id": "6a894bed-3ac4-4308-962c-a2bdfaa4c974", "__event_type__": "ToolCallEvent"}, {"timestamp": 1760777947.1833963, "text": "Now let me run the validation to check if the tests pass and meet the coverage requirements", "parent_progress_item_id": "6a894bed-3ac4-4308-962c-a2bdfaa4c974", "__event_type__": "UserVisibleModelOutputEvent"}, {"timestamp": 1760777947.7193086, "tool_name": "mcp__codespeak__validate_tests", "title": "mcp__codespeak__validate_tests", "details": null, "parent_progress_item_id": "6a894bed-3ac4-4308-962c-a2bdfaa4c974", "__event_type__": "ToolCallEvent"}, {"timestamp": 1760777948.0276003, "progress_item_id": "0f805778-df3f-4f8c-9e7a-11d75c452e60", "status": "Pending", "status_text": null, "title": "Running and validating tests (iteration 1)", "description": null, "parent_item_id": "9da6024a-3dbe-457e-8c7a-7bab8932bfd9", "__event_type__": "ProgressItemCreateEvent"}, {"timestamp": 1760777948.02766, "progress_item_id": "0f805778-df3f-4f8c-9e7a-11d75c452e60", "status": "In Progress", "status_text": null, "__event_type__": "ProgressItemUpdateEvent"}, {"timestamp": 1760777950.3577836, "progress_item_id": "0f805778-df3f-4f8c-9e7a-11d75c452e60", "status": "Done", "status_text": null, "__event_type__": "ProgressItemUpdateEvent"}, {"timestamp": 1760777950.3583176, "test_results": {"test_discovery_failure": null, "tests_summary": {"passed": 1, "failed": 0, "skipped": 0, "error": 0, "xfailed": 0, "xpassed": 0, "deselected": 0, "total": 1, "collected": 1}, "test_failures": [], "missing_line_coverage": [], "coverage_percentage_for_called_methods": null}, "__event_type__": "TestsRunEvent"}, {"timestamp": 1760777957.9758563, "text": "Perfect! The test validation has passed successfully. Let me summarize what I accomplished:\n\n## Summary\n\nI successfully implemented the required test coverage for the project:\n\n### Tests Added\n- **`test_main.py`**: Created a unit test for the `main` function in `src/test_build/main.py`\n  - **Test Method**: `test_main()` \n  - **Test Kind**: `unit_tests` (as specified in the requirements)\n  - **Test Description**: Tests that the `main()` function correctly prints \"Hello\" to stdout\n  - **Implementation**: Uses `unittest.mock.patch` to capture stdout and verifies the exact output\n  - **Timeout**: Added 30-second timeout as requested\n\n### Validation Results\n- \u2705 All tests pass validation\n- \u2705 Test coverage requirements are met\n- \u2705 No errors reported\n\nThe test follows the guidance for `unit_tests` by testing the public `main` method with simple inputs (no arguments needed) and asserting the expected output without using mocks for complex state or external APIs - only capturing stdout to verify the printed output.\n\nThe implementation is complete and all validation requirements have been satisfied.", "parent_progress_item_id": "6a894bed-3ac4-4308-962c-a2bdfaa4c974", "__event_type__": "UserVisibleModelOutputEvent"}, {"timestamp": 1760777958.5696983, "progress_item_id": "6a894bed-3ac4-4308-962c-a2bdfaa4c974", "status": "Done", "status_text": null, "__event_type__": "ProgressItemUpdateEvent"}, {"timestamp": 1760777958.7223914, "progress_item_id": "9da6024a-3dbe-457e-8c7a-7bab8932bfd9", "status": "Done", "status_text": null, "__event_type__": "ProgressItemUpdateEvent"}, {"timestamp": 1760777958.7379894, "text": "App built successfully.", "parent_progress_item_id": null, "__event_type__": "TextOutputEvent"}]